## 9. Future Expansion & Roadmap: Public Community & Analytics Portal

---

### 1. Vision & Concept Overview

To complement the administrative control plane, a high-performance, public-facing web portal can be deployed to showcase live network telemetry, leaderboard progression, and comprehensive player analytics. 

Because the backend operates across multiple Folia nodes and a Velocity proxy, the portal decouples telemetry ingestion from active game loops by querying an asynchronous time-series/relational analytics database rather than pinging game servers synchronously.


```

```
   ┌──────────────────┐       ┌──────────────────┐
   │   edge-proxy     │       │    folia-smp     │
   │ (Velocity Redis) │       │ (HuskSync MySQL) │
   └────────┬─────────┘       └────────┬─────────┘
            │                          │
            │ Events (Join/Quit/Stats) │
            ▼                          ▼
   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   │     Telemetry Ingestion Service / Redis     │
   └──────────────────────┬──────────────────────┘
                          │
                          ▼
   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   │           PostgreSQL / ClickHouse           │
   │    • Player Registry (UUID, Aliases)        │
   │    • Session History & Playtime Windows     │
   │    • Global & Regional Statistics           │
   └──────────────────────┬──────────────────────┘
                          │
                          ▼
   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   │ LXD Container: public-web-portal            │
   │ • Next.js / Astro Static-Edge Front End     │
   │ • Public REST & WebSocket Live APIs         │
   │ • Crafatar / Minotar 3D Avatar Rendering    │
   └─────────────────────────────────────────────┘

```

```

---

### 2. Core Feature Specifications

#### A. Live Pulse & Network Dashboard
* **Real-Time Player Manifest:** Visual grid of active players displaying 3D player heads/busts (rendered via Crafatar/Minotar integration), current server/dimension location (`Overworld`, `Nether`, `Lobby`), and active session duration.
* **Network Status & TPS:** Public-facing health gauges showing total online count relative to the 250-player cap, uptime metrics, and regional tick health.
* **Proximity Map Link:** Embedded deep links directly into the `BlueMap` 3D isometric viewer centered on active public landmarks.

#### B. Historical Player Registry & Global Directory
* **Universal Search Index:** Searchable registry of every player who has ever joined the server by username or Minecraft UUID, including history of known username changes.
* **Lifetime Playtime Tracking:** Aggregate playtime counters broken down by dimension (e.g., hours spent in the Overworld vs. Nether vs. End).
* **First Seen / Last Seen Timestamps:** Exact join history with relative time formatting (`Joined 4 months ago`, `Last active 12 minutes ago`).

#### C. Progression & Gameplay Leaderboards
* **AuraSkills Leaderboards:** Global rankings for individual skill levels (Farming, Mining, Combat, Agility) and Total Power Level.
* **Economic Analytics:** Richest players/guilds, top auction house traders, and market velocity stats derived from `AxAuctions` / `Vault-Unlocked` database state.
* **In-Game Milestones:** Trackers for blocks mined, mob/boss kills (Ender Dragon, Wither), player deaths, and total distance traveled via Elytra/boat.

#### D. Personal Player Profile Pages (`/player/[uuid]`)
* **Player Showcase Card:** Customizable profile card displaying equipped armor, holding item, and active skin render.
* **Activity Heatmaps:** GitHub-style daily activity contribution charts showing playtime frequency over the past 365 days.
* **Land Claim Badges:** List of public claims/settlements owned via `HuskClaims` with teleportation coordinates.

---

### 3. Architecture & Tech Stack

| Layer | Recommended Technology | Role |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Ingestion Pipeline** | Go / Python Daemon + Redis Pub/Sub | Consumes disconnect/connect packets from Velocity and stat dumps from Folia nodes. |
| **Analytics Storage** | PostgreSQL or SQLite (with Litestream) | Stores persistent player profiles, session logs, and leaderboard aggregates. |
| **Frontend Framework**| Next.js (App Router) or Astro | Server-side rendered (SSR) pages for instant SEO, fast initial load, and responsive Tailwind UI. |
| **Skin / Avatar API** | Crafatar / Visage Cache | Local caching proxy for player head renders and isometric body avatars to avoid external rate limits. |
| **Container Hosting** | Dedicated LXD Container (`public-web`) | Pinned to E-Cores (Cores 10–11) to guarantee zero CPU contention with main SMP tick loops. |

---

